            <ArticleTitle>Steroid-responsive tubular aggregate myopathy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>233-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a man with an acute myalgia/cramp syndrome and tubular aggregates on his muscle biopsy. He was placed on prednisone and was found to be exquisitely sensitive to the drug, with changes of only 5 mg precipitating recurrence of symptoms. He was eventually tapered off all steroids, without symptoms, and repeat biopsy showed no tubular aggregates. We recommend similar patients be given a trial of high-dose steroids.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
